.TH SPITOOL 1 "2026-10-09" "spitool 0.99" "spintent"
.SH NAME
spitool \- clean luamml ghost characters and validate tagged PDF files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spitool
.RI [ options ]
.IR file ...
.br
.B spitool
.B \-h
|
.B \-\-help
.br
.B spitool
.B \-v
|
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spitool
is a
.BR texlua (1)
script distributed with the
.B spintent
LaTeX package.
It prepares the MathML produced by
.B luamml
for the associated-files (math-AF) mode of a tagged PDF, and checks
that the tag structure and the PDF/UA-2 conformance of a document are
correct.
.PP
The package
.B spintent
can write invisible marker characters (U+2063, with the attribute
.B sptmp
set to
.B outer
or
.BR inner )
in the MathML that
.B luamml
produces.
They protect the structure of the formulas, but must not remain in the
MathML file that is attached to the PDF.
.B spitool
removes them from the HTML file written by
.BR luamml ,
which is named
.IB name \-luamml\-mathml.html \fR,
and leaves the result as
.IB name \-mathml.html \fR.
.PP
What
.B spitool
does with each
.I file
depends on its extension; see
.BR MODES .
Several files may be given; they are processed in order.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B .pdf
The file is only validated; nothing is compiled and nothing is written.
Two checks are run, each one only if its tools are found in
.BR PATH :
the tag structure is dumped with
.B show-pdf-tags \-\-xml
and verified with
.BR rnv-wrapp ,
and the PDF/UA-2 conformance is verified with
.B verapdf \-\-flavour ua2.
The result is reported as
.B PASS
or
.BR FAIL ,
and the output of the failing validator is shown.
If neither pair of tools is found, the run ends with an error.
.TP
.B .html
The file must be named
.IB name \-luamml\-mathml.html \fR.
The ghost characters are removed and the result is written as
.IB name \-mathml.html \fR.
.TP
.BR .tex ", " .ltx
The document is compiled once with the TeX engine, in a private temporary
directory, with the option
.B AFghost=true
passed to the package
.BR spintent ,
so that
.B luamml
writes the ghost characters in the HTML file.
The HTML file is then cleaned as in the
.B .html
mode.
Afterwards, if the validators are available, the PDF just produced is
validated as in the
.B .pdf
mode.
That PDF stays in the temporary directory and is discarded; only the
cleaned HTML file is kept.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check\-only ", " \-\-test\-only
Do not compile anything; only validate PDF files.
With this option every
.I file
must be a PDF file.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-overwrite
Replace the output file
.IB name \-mathml.html
if it already exists.
Without this option
.B spitool
refuses to overwrite it and stops with an error.
It has no effect together with
.BR \-c ,
and a warning is printed.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path =\fIpath\fR
Write the output file in the directory
.IR path ,
which is created, with its parents, if it does not exist.
The file is named after the document alone, without the directory of the
input file.
It has no effect together with
.BR \-c ,
and a warning is printed.
The forms
.BI \-p\  path
and
.BI \-\-path\  path
are also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-engine =\fIcmd\fR
TeX engine used to compile the
.B .tex
and
.B .ltx
files.
By default it is
.B lualatex\-dev
if it is found in
.BR PATH ,
and
.B lualatex
otherwise.
The name may contain only letters, digits, dots, underscores and hyphens.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-strict
Stop at the first failure, either of the compilation or of a validation.
Without this option all the files are processed.
In both cases the exit status is not zero if anything failed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the usage and exit.
This is also what happens when
.B spitool
is run without arguments from an interactive terminal.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version number and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; the remaining arguments are file names.
.SH FILE NAMES
If a
.I file
does not exist as given, its extension may be omitted: with
.B \-c
the extension
.B .pdf
is tried; otherwise
.BR .tex ,
.BR .ltx ,
.BR .pdf ,
.B \-luamml\-mathml.html
and
.BR .html ,
in this order.
.PP
For safety, a file name containing spaces, quotes or any of the
characters
.B % & | < > ^ ` $ { } [ ] ! # ~
is rejected, since the name is passed to the shell and to TeX.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB name \-mathml.html
Output file with the ghost characters removed.
It is written next to the input file, or in the directory given with
.BR \-\-path .
If no ghost character is found a warning is printed and the file is not
kept; it usually means that
.B spintent
was not loaded or that the HTML file was not produced with
.BR AFghost=true .
.TP
.IB name \-luamml\-mathml.html
Input of the
.B .html
mode; it is written by
.B luamml
and is never modified.
.TP
.BI spitool\- XXXXXX
Temporary directory of the
.B .tex
and
.B .ltx
modes, created with mode 700 inside
.BR $TMPDIR .
It is removed at the end.
If the compilation fails it is kept, and its location is shown, so that
the log file can be read.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory where the temporary directory is created on POSIX systems
(default
.BR /tmp ).
On Windows
.B TEMP
or
.BR TMP
is used instead.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All the files were processed and no compilation or validation failed.
Finding no ghost character is only a warning.
.TP
.B 1
A file could not be found or is not valid, an option is wrong, an
output file already exists and
.B \-\-overwrite
was not given, or a compilation or a validation failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a PDF file, without compiling:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ spitool \-c sample.pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
The same, with the extension omitted and stopping at the first failure:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ spitool \-c \-s sample
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile a document with the ghost characters enabled, write the cleaned
MathML in the directory
.B build
(replacing it if it exists) and validate the PDF:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ spitool \-o \-p build/ sample.tex
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean an HTML file that was already written by
.BR luamml :
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ spitool sample\-luamml\-mathml.html
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lualatex (1),
.BR texlua (1),
.BR verapdf (1)
.PP
